// generate-bmc-tools-suite.js
// Generates the "BMC vendor tools" suite under the Remote Management tab: Dell racadm (iDRAC),
// HPE iLOrest (iLO), Supermicro SAA, Lenovo OneCLI (XCC), GNU FreeIPMI and serial consoles
// (picocom, ser2net, conserver), plus the bmc-tools.html hub.
//
// Facts checked 2026-11-07 against official sources:
// - Dell iDRAC9 7.x RACADM CLI Guide (getsysinfo, getversion, getsel, clrsel, lclog, hwinventory,
//   storage, serveraction, get/set, jobqueue, techsupreport, update, racreset, getsensorinfo).
//   The guide documents only -p for remote passwords (no prompt, no env var). No iDRAC10 RACADM
//   guide was reachable, so iDRAC10 differences are not covered.
// - HPE iLOrest 7.4.0.0 user guide (changelog, global, iLO, repository and storage commands).
// - Supermicro SAA for UEFI User's Guide rev 1.1.0 (Aug 28, 2024; "formerly known as SUM") and
//   Supermicro FAQ 42925 (out-of-band -l list form). The OS build's full guide was not
//   reachable: options beyond those are marked "check saa -h".
// - Lenovo XClarity Essentials OneCLI 5.7.0 docs (global parameters, config, update, misc).
// - GNU FreeIPMI 1.6.20 (Oct 5, 2026) and the freeipmi-tools man pages; ser2net 4.6.8 README and
//   ser2net.yaml(5); conserver 8.3.0 (Feb 2, 2026) console(1) and conserver.cf(5); picocom(1).
// Menu logos: official marks from Simple Icons 15.0.0 (CC0): Dell, Supermicro, Lenovo; GNU mark
// for FreeIPMI (a GNU project). HPE is not in Simple Icons: its logo is the HPE Element, a green
// rectangle, drawn here in HPE green (#01A982).
//
// Re-runnable: sheet .js files are rewritten every run; .html files are only created when
// missing; the menu is replaced if present (build-nav-groups.js then files it under its tab).
const { buildSuite } = require('./generate-suite-kit');

